==Battleground==
*1 [[Dark Cyclone]] spawns after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>.
*1 [[White Cyclone]] spawns after 42 seconds<sup>1,260f</sup>.
*1 [[Red Cyclone]] spawns after 44 seconds<sup>1,320f</sup>.
*1 [[Divine Cyclone]] spawns after 46 seconds<sup>1,380f</sup>.
*1 [[Cosmic Cyclone]] spawns after 48 seconds<sup>1,440f</sup>.
*1 [[Zyclone]] spawns after 50 seconds<sup>1,500f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This level isn't as hard as it first seems, since all of the Cyclones have low range and are susceptible to CC effects. A large number of spammable units can simply overrun the stage with proper deployment. Due to the tight startoff and the fact that a Cyclone drops enough funds for a full restock, a Rich Cat is highly recommended.

Because none of the Cyclones here are bosses, bringing enough knockback units to cover every trait here (i.e. [[Fortune Teller Cat (Rare Cat)|Fisherman Cat]], [[Stilts Cat (Rare Cat)|Totem Cat]], [[Li'l Gross Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Macho Legs]]) will allow you to [[cheese]] the stage by knocking all the Cyclones back behind the enemy base so other units can simply destroy it.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo]] - Without Sanzo, this stage is nigh impossible, whose rapid, short-ranged area attacks can slow Floating (and Angel with Talents) threats, helping to control most of the Cyclones in the stage. However, it only barely outranges Cosmic Cyclone (240 vs 250), and something else needs to be reserved for Zyclone. Use him with research combos.
*[[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman]] - A spammable melee DPS unit, Cameraman is an essential component of any strategy, being strong against Floating at Sanzo's range and has 50% chance to survive a lethal strike. With talents, she will always survive such hits, and in numbers, she can simply overwhelm them with sheer weight of fire if supported properly.
*[[Psychocat (Rare Cat)|Corrupted Psychocat]] - A midranger CC unit who primarily finds applications against Cosmic Cyclone, standing at a comfortable 365 range. If talented with Target Zombie the unit also helps out with Zyclone.
*[[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife]] - While more frequently used for LD DPS rather than her CC, Housewife does have access to the Savage Blow talent for even more mayhem, 50% chance to slow Zombies for 5 seconds to counter Zyclone and Zombie Killer if she lands the last hit.
*[[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk]] - Augmented by talents, Cyberpunk's LD attacks can slow all enemies in the stage from a massive 1200 range for 4 seconds, buying the other CC units much more breathing room.
*[[Freshman Cat Jobs (Super Rare Cat)|Headmaster Cat Jobs]] - Due to the lack of non-cyclone type enemies, Headmaster Cat Jobs's pulverizing match up against cyclones leads to it making this stage nearly free. True form is essential if you decide to use Cat Jobs, due to its higher speed and surge attack. However, do note that the surge spawn location is incredibly inconsistent, so do not rely solely on catjobs if you decide to bring him.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[The Grateful Crane (Uber Rare Cat)|The Grateful Crane]]: With his low cost and quick recharge, he essentially acts as another spammable crowd-controller. He also has a [[Cat Combo]] with [[Ninja Cat (Special Cat)|Ninja Cat]] that increases knockback, which can help if other knockback units like [[Ancient Egg: N105 (Rare Cat)|Racquet Cat]] and [[Welterweight Cat (Rare Cat)|Ectoweight Cat]] are used.
*[[Shining Amaterasu (Uber Rare Cat)|Almighty Amaterasu]] - A backliner with massive damage to all things traited, Amaterasu can comfortably stay behind and dish out substantial amounts of damage once in a while. With [[Talents]], she even gets Zombie Killer, allowing her to finish off Zyclone by herself.
*[[Mighty Rekon Korps (Uber Rare Cat)|Orbital Annihilator Ragnarok]] - Targeting only traited enemies, Ragnarok packs a serious punch with each attack at 470 range. Its long attack animation allowing the cyclones to get within striking range, and it has Zombie Killer to terminate Zyclone for good.
*[[Tecoluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Lufalan Pasalan]] - A single-target nuker with a massive 720 range and incredible damage, Lufalan finds a comfortable matchup with multiple strong targets that it can constantly whittle away while the CC units keep the Cyclones in check. Its critical hits are not to be relied upon, but does speed up the stage when it occurs.
*[[Skull Rider Vars (Uber Rare Cat)|Halloween Knight Vars]]: His almost 100% Knockback and Slow uptime in his cheap true form are very useful against Zyclone and Cosmic Cyclone, the two cyclones that Sanzo doesn't counter very well.
*[[Juri (Uber Rare Cat)|Juri CC]]: Juri's ability to crowd-control floating enemies with her Long Range will wreck havoc on the Cyclones.

